S
#17464
The Smithy~
   Ever wonder what happened to those gold and silver coins that you somehow
lost or dropped a long the way?  This is where they end up.  The faerie Smithy
gathers them up and works his famous magic to flatten, bend and shape the coins
in to beautiful and magical faerie armor.    
~
174 8 0 0 0 0 255 0
D0
~
~
0 0 17456
S
#17465
The Bookworm Shop~
   Faeries are ever so curious and love to learn.  They also love to teach and
tell stories.  In this shop you will find all the writing tools and paper you
will need to help you put your tales to the world.    
~
174 8 0 0 0 0 255 0
D0
~
~
0 0 17459
S
#17466
The Grand Oak Pub~
   This magnificent Oak tree is over 500 years old.  Fashioned from the Oak
tree, its shining floors, long, stein-covered bars and intricately-carved
stools make you just want a drink yourself.  You elbow your way through the
crowd that always fills this pub, and have a good look around.  Tapestries
adorn the walls, as do portraits of faerie of bygone years.  An Elk horn
chandelier hangs from high above your head and you estimate that at least 500
fire flies must be sitting upon it.    
~
