#17471
A Subterranean Abode~
   You have stepped into a small quaint dwelling of some sort.  The entire
place is carved out of the thick root system.  The fact no vegetation has been
harmed is amazing.  The ceiling is a virtual latticework of woven roots, and
provide for a perfect view of the forest above without revealing the location
of the hovel.  The atmosphere is cozy and warming, but the place is a literal
mess.  Drawings, maps, books, and loose paper riddled with writing and
scribbling is strewn about.  Whomever calls this place home is evidently way to
busy to pick up the clutter.    
~
